{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he said to them: No; rather, you have come to see the nakedness of the land.</b> Now I say that 'you have come to see the nakedness of the land' is an argument in its own right and does not depend on the charge 'you are spies.' For at first I made this argument merely a support to the charge 'you are spies,' since without it I would have said that perhaps you have no connection one with another and met by chance together within the city. But now that you have come to explain the hidden matter and to say that you are all brothers and that you fear the evil eye — if so, I see that your gathering is no chance matter. And if so, why did you enter through ten gates of the city? Surely it is because you have come to see the nakedness of the land."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:00.862150559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}